--- reading it --------------------------------------------------------------------------
Result: PASS for the feeder half of FR-032. With the userspace feeder gone and the device left armed
("watchdog did not stop!" is the kernel saying the close carried no magic character), the board reset
itself 25 s later, inside the 30 s margin (the last feed was up to 5 s before the kill), booted the same
slot and confirmed it. Nobody touched it; the "ll" at 21:25:50 was typed after the banner appeared.

Also shown:
1. The kernel carries omap_wdt.early_enable=1 on its command line, from the built-in CONFIG_CMDLINE,
   and the slot's root= is still the slot's own (/dev/mmcblk0p3).
2. The kernel command line is the bootloader's arguments FOLLOWED BY the built-in string, not the
   other way round (drivers/of/fdt.c appends CONFIG_CMDLINE with strlcat), which is the opposite of
   what the Kconfig help says. Research R5 said the built-in string came first and was wrong; it is
   corrected there. The consequence is stronger than the text had it: anything in CONFIG_CMDLINE is
   read last and wins over U-Boot's root= and console=, so the old built-in "root=/dev/mmcblk0p2"
   would have made slot B boot slot A's root filesystem, and it was right to replace it.
3. The ota-health line is printed on the boot that follows the reset, so the watchdog reset did not
   leave the slot unconfirmed: a healthy slot that was hit once returns to service on its own.
4. The ota-clock floor is now the build time of fb19ed4 (11:03:45), the running slot's, as designed.

NOT shown by this capture: the kernel-hang half (echo c > /proc/sysrq-trigger, at most 60 s), and
scenario B (a slot that never confirms is reset about every two minutes and retired after the third
attempt, SC-014). T032 and T034 stay open until those two are on record.

